A||||21||Richard Parnell||Indexing sparkplugs||||5||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||12-24-1999||08:30 PM||||Has anyone heard of indexing spark plugs so they face toward the intake valve? Where would you get the washers to do this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||12-24-1999||08:54 PM||||Think about this!<BR>The intake valves are open on the downstroke of the pistons intake stroke. The sparkplug fires near the top of the compression stroke.  I would think that the air-fuel mixture would be fairly even through out the combustion chamber at this point and the gap facing the closed intake would do zilch. If anything indexing toward the center of the cylinder would be better, and would probably be little if any improvement in burn rate or efficiency.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2FAST4U||12-24-1999||10:27 PM||||You can get ingexing washers at just about any speed shop or online at jegs.com or summitracing.com<P>Merry Xmas<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000003||mutfish||12-24-1999||11:30 PM||||Spark plug indexing is used in full boogie race motors and would be negligible on a high performance street engine at best, let alone the power plants in our little toys.  It is usually done to start the flame kernal at a specific point in the combustion chamber or to avoid the ground electrode on the sparkplug in super high compression engines........||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||12-29-1999||02:27 PM||||Indexing is done to point the electrode gap toward the center of the combustion chamber.  <P>Use a marker to put a line on the outside of the plug opposite the electrode "arm".  This mark neeeds to point to the center of the combustion chamber when the plug is installed.  Try swapping the plugs around to get all the marks to line up before you buy indexing washers.  Each plug is a little different.<P>Put you car on a dyno and rejoice at the incredible power gained (.5 hp), maybe.<P>When racing for $$$$ every tiny little bit helps.  Races are won by .001 thousandth of a second.  For street use you'll never know the difference.  <P>The next time you do the plugs try it, but don't dwell on it or waste $ or time on it.||||reg||12
Z||000005||2FAST4U||12-29-1999||03:02 PM||||A 1/2 HP here a 1/2 HP there and soon they add up to a good running car. When you don't have cubic inches to make power you use finesse. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-30-1999||12:56 AM||||I don't think it would be worth the hassle.  I was thinking that, if you really want to index you sparkplugs, they should go somewhere between "spank" and "spartan".||||reg||1
