Z||000009||dogtired||12-30-1999||06:39 AM||||MonkeyMan, I am sure I could tell you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Now lets think about this indexing thing a little more, for our street machines?<BR>Isn't that a little like Waxing your car to cut down on wind resistance???<BR>And all of us, including me, who has a wing on the back, to provide down force, which has very little functionality untill you reach speeds of 130 MPH plus, I do that every day on the way to work???<BR>OK OK Just some of MY thoughts.<BR>I think its time to go change the air in my tires again, its getting stale, so its hard to roll  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000010||Greg Piet||12-30-1999||08:51 AM||||Im glad I am not the only one thinking this was a bit extreme.  I was thinking that removing the passenger seat/spare tire, radio, carpet, subwoofer,etc...  to reduce weight would be more of a performance boost than worrying about the position of your spark plug electrode.   Well one way of getting around indexing i would think would be to go to the Bosch +4 's that way you only have 90 degrees to alter the electrode position rather than 360 with a standard plug||||reg||1
