Z||000014||batboy||12-30-1999||03:32 PM||||I seriously doubt a 5 HP increase. I'd like to see the dyno numbers. It's purely racing stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Phil||12-30-1999||03:54 PM||||I see a lot of HP increase figures thrown out for different mods with no backup data. I wouldn't be suprised if all these 20HP increases turned out to be 1 or 2 HP. There was a web site that did dyno runs after every mod they made and the HP increases were not that great. I think headers were something like 8HP not the 25 everybody quotes.It was quite the eye opener. I had the opportunity to see a bunch of cars dynoed this fall and many HP claims were greatly revised after the numbers came in even accounting for the approx. 15-20% loss thru the drivetrain. So like Batboy says "I'd like to see the dyno numbers"||||reg||1
Z||000016||Greg Piet||12-30-1999||05:27 PM||||Richard,<BR>I dont want to give the impression of "bashing" you or anyone else.  Please keep throwing out tidbits as it may help someone.  (Hey if someday i actually have a "race car" fiero i might remember to index the plugs from this thread for a little xtra power)||||reg||1
Z||000017||Phil||12-30-1999||06:13 PM||||There was a segment on Inside Winston Cup awhile back about spark plugs. They said that they use plugs without the electrode arm. My outboard(200 Merc) had plugs without the arm. No I'm not saying my boat had racing plugs but such critters do exist.||||reg||1
Z||000018||theogre||12-30-1999||10:01 PM||||I can't remember who, accell I think, was genereally of the oppinion that indexing is mostly a waste of time. even on race motors they had a hard time measuring any dif.||||reg||1
Z||000019||mutfish||01-01-2000||10:35 AM||||On a spark plug related topic,a while back I read a dyno test of the Split-Fire spark plugs.The test mule was a small block ford,and it actually lost 2-3 hp.useing them.<P>If it ain't broke don't fix it?..........||||reg||1
Z||000020||JIM GOOSE||01-03-2000||04:44 PM||||I got started indexing the plugs on my KAW 1000 using the MOROSO kit which is 3 diff tck washers and a test block. These plugs are easy to get to after the tank is off and theres only 4 of em. Sometimes, you have to try all 3 washers and still don't get a perfect alignment. Hard to tell about HP increase but it seems to help and the KAW likes fresh plugs anyway bout every 1000 m.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Phil||01-03-2000||04:50 PM||||2 strokes can be a whole different animal when it comes to plugs.||||reg||1
